Flashback
[Twenty years ago...]

[The old Mystery Inc. enters an abandoned chapel.]

Judy: Are you sure that thing came in here, Brad?

Brad: It's the only place it could have gone.

Ricky: For real, maybe we should call the local Smokey to handle this.

Cassidy: Ricky's right. That thing didn't look exactly... human. It had horns.

Pericles: The real question is, did we chase it here, or were we led here on purpose?

[A shadow flies by. Pericles flies after it.]

Ricky: Professor Pericles! No! Come back! [runs after Pericles, steps on organ]

[Ricky climbs onto the organ, but the pipes bend and fall over.]

Pericles: [flies back down] False alarm. It was just a possum. Mm, delicious.

[Cassidy glares at Ricky.]

Ricky: Sorry. [spots scroll] Whoa, far out! What's that?

Brad: [opens scroll] What is this?

Pericles: No idea, but I can't wait to find out.

[A monster observes them from a distance.]

Monster: From six to one, the spell is spun. No time to run, the curse begun.

[Theme song plays]

INT. K-Ghoul - Day
[Shaggy and Scooby cook in the kitchen.]

Angel: What are you clowns doing to my kitchen?

Shaggy: [chuckles] We're just makin' breakfast, dude!

Scooby: Yeah, gotta start the day off right!

Angel: If somethin' living crawls from that pot, I will not hesitate to devastate, dig? [to Velma] So, how's it goin' with your, uh...

Velma: Planispheric Disk? That's what Pericles called it. To answer your question, not good. None of these symbols make sense. I was hoping maybe you knew something, because of... you know... who you really are?

Angel: Sorry, baby. I wish I could help.

[Fred and Daphne are outside.]

Daphne: Oh, Freddy, just think. A couple of months from now, we'll be engaged.

Fred: [busy managing Mystery Machine] Uh-huh.

Daphne: I want to break the news to everyone just right. Something big, but not tacky.

Fred: Yup.

Daphne: And it has to be better than what my sisters did, especially Dawn. I mean, please! How hard is it to train chickens to spell out your name? All you need is some corn and electrical wire. Huh! [no response from Fred] Fred, are you even listening to me?

Fred: [sighs] Sorry, Daph. The Mystery Machine is a mess! Nothing is where it should be! But... I have got a plan! [takes out cellphone] I downloaded an app for my smartphone that tells me whenever some of my equipment has been moved. Check it out.

[Fred moves a wire to a wrong shelf. The cellphone makes a burping noise.]

Fred: Isn't that awesome?!

[Daphne sighs.]

Scooby: [comes out with Shaggy carrying a plate of food] Come and get it!

Shaggy: Might be heavy on the caramel, but Scoob found some hot sauce that should cut that!

Velma: [reads bottle] "Cabeza fuego?"

Scooby: It means "fire head."

Velma: I know what it- jinkies! That's it! [runs into trailer]

Shaggy: Like, did she get sick of the food already? She didn't even taste it.

[Velma comes out with the piece and looks at it through the Mystery Machine's side-view mirror.]

Velma: I couldn't figure out the writing on the disk because it was backwards... and in Spanish! [reveals "FUEGO" on disk]

Daphne: Wait, that trunk I was sitting on... check it out! Aren't there Spanish books in there?

Fred: That's the trunk we found at Darrow College, with the stuff about the town!

[They find an envelope with Mr. E's seal on it inside. Fred gasps.]

All: Mr. E!

[Daphne opens the envelope and an audio plays.]

Mr. E (audio): Greetings, Mystery Incorporated! In order to truly decipher what lies within, you will need to begin where this mystery ended.

Fred: Of course! Gang, get that trunk in the van. We're going back to school, and I know just who can help us!

INT. Darrow Library
Hatecraft: No! Sorry, can't help! Now is just not a good time.

[A shush is heard offscreen]

Shaggy: Oh, come on, Professor Hatecraft. You're like, the only teacher we know here besides Harlan Ellison.

Scooby: That guy scares me!

Velma: Besides, Harlan's away on sabbatical at a misanthropes convention.

Hatecraft: Which is precisely my problem. With Harlan away, Dean Fenk has replaced him with a new professor, Regina Wentworth. [shows her books]

Daphne: The author of the Dusk teen vampire romance series? Oh my gosh! I've read them all. Dusk, Dusk: Early Evening, Dusk: Just Before Bedtime, Forbidden Love, Hidden Desire... Fred, those books are so us! Just with less bloodletting.

Librarian: Shh!

[Hatecraft leads Mystery Inc. outside.]

EXT. Courtyard - Evening
Hatecraft: Since the scandal discrediting my last novel, Char Gar Gothakon: The Beast that Hath no Name, my books haven't been selling. To please Dean Fenk, I've been trying my hand writing a teen vampire novel, but I have no idea what teens these days do.

Fred: Well, that's easy. We're into solving mysteries and building traps!

Velma: Why don't we let us help you?

Shaggy: Like, yeah! We've been teenagers forever!

Daphne: And in return, you can help us decipher the papers in our trunk!

Hatecraft: You'd do that, for me?

Fred: Sure! And don't worry, professor. The dean won't even know we were here.

[The Mystery Machine suddenly explodes. A masked woman comes out.]

Obliteratrix: I am the Obliteratrix, and I have but one purpose: to destroy Mystery Incorporated!

[Scene cuts]

Shaggy: Zoinks! [whimpers] She killed the Mystery Machine!

Velma: And the trunk!

Fred: And my track gear!

Daphne: Forget about that!

Scooby: Run!

[They run, but the Obliteratrix shoots lasers blocking their path.]

Shaggy: Like, not only does this chick really hate us, but she's not human! She's...

Scooby: A ghost assassin!

Hatecraft: Up ahead! We can lose her in there!

[They run into a busy lecture hall.]

Fred: We lost her. Way to go, professor.

Velma: Where are we?

[They are in Wentworth's novel reading.]

Hatecraft: Uh-oh.

EXT. Courtyard - Evening
Reporter: I'm here with Natasha Fenk, dean of Darrow College, and beautiful teen romance writer, Regina Wentworth. Ladies, any idea what happened?

Fenk: We're investigating.

Regina: Oh, please! It was obviously that creep, H.P. Hatecraft. Jealous much, Mr. Oldie-Olderson Writer? [laughs]

[Mystery Inc. and Hatecraft watch from the distance in horror.]

Hatecraft: This is just the excuse Fenk has been waiting for to get rid of me.

Scooby: Why would this... Obb... [struggles to pronounce name] ...whatever, want to destroy us?

Velma: What if it wasn't us, but what we had?

Daphne: You mean, that trunk full of clues?

Shaggy: Like, that could mean the Obliterakusa, er, the Obliteratrix, isn't an undead assasin at all!

Fred: Well, whoever she is, she messed with the wrong van. The Mystery Machine will be avenged!

INT. Mr. E's Headquarters
[Cassidy, Mr. E, and Ed Machine watch the aftermath from their headquarters.]

Cassidy: This has that flying rat Pericles' wingprints all over it!

Mr. E: Possible, albeit a little sloppy for him. We'll wait and see.

Cassidy: Wait and see? The kids are in danger!

Mr. E: Ed will look into it. But no interfering, unless necessary.

Cassidy: I don't like this, E.

Mr. E: Understood, but let's not forget, little Angel, I brought you back to Crystal Cove. We're both in this together, remember?

INT. Darrow Library/Hatecraft's House - Night
Velma: Without the Darrow files, we're pretty much starting from scratch. I'll take the Spanish section. Daphne, Crystal Cove history. And Fred...

Daphne: [hugs Fred] Will come with me. [quietly to Fred] We can discuss the you-know-what while we're looking.

Fred: Cool, I've got some great ideas!

Daphne: You do? Oh, Freddy! [they exit]

Velma: Ugh, wish I'd gone with Shaggy and Scoob.

[Meanwhile, at Hatecraft's house, Shaggy and Scooby go in with Hatecraft]

Hatecraft: Thank you for agreeing to help me with my novel.

Scooby: No problem!

Hatecraft: Forgive the mess. I've been trying to get more into the spirit of a teenage girl. I've tentatively called my novel The Disinternment of Groth van Anuroth. Yo, yo, yo. What do you think? Too urban?

Shaggy: Oh, boy.

[Back at the library, Fred speaks with Daphne.]

Fred: So that's my idea: an engagement trap. Now, all we need is a place big enough to contain our friends and family. Does Crystal Cove have a missile silo?

Daphne: [growls] Enough! Couldn't we just tell everyone over a nice brunch?

Velma: [sarcastically] I can see you two are searching hard. Come on, I think I found something.

[Scene cuts to history book showing Planispheric Disk]

Velma: Recognize anything?

Daphne: That drawing. It looks like...

Fred: Our disk piece. Only...

Velma: It's complete.

Daphne: [reads] Spanish conquistadors used the Planispheric Disk to navigate uncharted oceans, and sometimes to hide their cargo so it could be found later.

Velma: Cargo like a haunted treasure! Questions are, what is the treasure, and where are the other pieces of the disk?

[Fred's smartphone burps.]

Daphne: Ew, Freddy!

Fred: That wasn't me! It was my smartphone. That's the sound my trap-tracker makes, but that's impossible unless... the Mystery Machine is alive!

[Scene cuts back to Hatecraft's house]

Hatecraft: [reads draft] I knew the moment I saw the school's teen vampire hottie in biology class, he was the One. His cleft chin was like the mall of Torgon, the beast that hammers me wild. His name... was Barry.

Shaggy: Okay, like, stop. Barry? Dude, you need a real teen name, like Shaggy!

Scooby: And where's the food, H.P.? Sheesh!

[The door knocks. It is Fred's group. Hatecraft answers the door.]

Fred: Professor Hatecraft! We think the Mystery Machine might still be alive, but we need to track it down. Do you have a car?

Hatecraft: No. But I know where we can get one.

EXT. Trainyard - Night
[They drive a truck promoting Dusk to the trainyard. Daphne walks out with a cutout.]

Daphne: I wonder what Fred would look like with fangs and skin the colour of boiled pork.

Fred: [follows tracker] Everybody, follow me! According to my tracker, the Mystery Machine should be right in front of us!

Daphne: But this is just an old train!

Velma: Or is it? [moves curtain, revealing Mystery Machine]

All: The Mystery Machine!

Shaggy: But, like, why would the... whatever her name is, fake blowing it up and then hide it here?

Obliteratrix: [offscreen] To lure you into a trap.

Shaggy: Oh, right. That makes... [realizes, shudders] Zoinks!

[The Obliteratrix jumps onto a train car and takes out a bow and arrow.]

Shaggy: Like, where does she keep getting these weapons? That outfit has no pockets!

Velma: Run!

[The Obliteratrix fires an explosive arrow. They retreat into a train car to avoid the explosion.]

Fred: In here! [pulls Daphne and Velma in just before explosion]

Hatecraft: Does anyone else notice that the Obliteratrix is in great shape? [Mystery Inc. looks at each other confused] I was just trying to point out that the same could be said for Regina. Coincidence?

Daphne: But why would Regina Wentworth want us dead?

Fred: We'll figure that out later. Right now, we need to get to the Mystery Machine so I can rig one of my traps. Come on!

[They run to the Mystery Machine. Fred takes the box of supplies from the trunk, but the Obliteratrix, hiding through invisibility, appears and fires arrows at Fred. She misses, blowing up a train car. As Mystery Inc. continues running, she throws grenades and finally kicks what she believes is a victim, but is really just the cutout.]

Fred: [hiding under train car] Now, Scooby!

[Scooby presses a button, springing a trap meant to crush the Obliteratrix.]

Fred: Time to see who we caught.

[Scooby lifts up the sheet, but finds only the broken cutout.]

EXT. Trainyard - Night
[Fenk, Wentworth, and the police are here to see the aftermath.]

Fenk: I want Hatecraft arrested! He stole a school property!

Regina: [holds up broken cutout] And he broke Todd!

Sheriff: Alright, ladies, enough. First things first, tell me more about the super hot Obliteratrix girl. Is she, uh... single?

Fenk: [to Hatecraft] You're fired! Pack your office and be gone by morning. Come on, Regina.

Regina: Good luck with your career, H.P. Buttcraft! [exits, laughing]

Hatecraft: My life is over. As Shagoth Godar would say, oh, the tentacles of Agalbor have eaten my entrails, and Glargle my liver.

INT. Motel - Night
[Pericles watches remotely from a no-tell motel.]

Pericles: Well, Mystery Incorporated, it appears you've made an enemy. Fortunately for you, I still require you... [turns TV off] alive.

INT. Hatecraft's House - Night
[Mystery Inc. opens the archives.]

Fred: The Darrow archives. Start digging, gang.

Velma: I've been through the trunk a bunch of times. It's mostly stuff about the conquistadors who founded Crystal Cove, the haunted treasure...

Hatecraft: Wait, here's something. Several documents reference coloro vidrio— coloured glass, and ore, which means pray.

Shaggy: Like, who would pray to coloured glass?

Daphne: What if "coloured glass" means stained glass, like at church?

Scooby: Oh, oh! Aphrodite! And Pericles!

Fred: Right, Scoob! Pericles stole the conquistador's map when Aphrodite attacked the town! A map that was in...

INT. Chapel - Night
All: ...the old Spanish church!

[They all enter.]

Fred: Okay. Everyone, start looking for clues.

[Shaggy and Scooby look in the confession booth but find rats inside. Daphne breaks a floorboard, revealing a secret compartment with a matching locket.]

Daphne: Gang, look at this! It's identical to the locket I found in the caves!

Velma: The original Mystery Incorporated must have been here!

Fred: We're getting close. Start digging. Maybe there's more clues.

Hatecraft: Uh, where are Shaggy and Scooby?

[The rats chase Shaggy and Scooby out of the booth.]

Shaggy: It's on me! It's on me!

[Fred steps back but accidentally steps on a tile, opening a secret trapdoor.]

Velma: Jinkies! This hole probably goes straight down to the Crystal Cove Mines.

Fred: Must have been hidden for decades.

Daphne: I wonder if anyone else knows about this.

Obliteratrix: No, it's a secret that will die with all of you! Tonight!

Scooby: She's back!

Fred: Don't worry, Scoob! This time, I'm one trap ahead of her!

[A claw springs, but the Obliteratrix destroys it. Fred dodges the falling debris, but the Obliteratrix drops nets capturing all of them except Hatecraft.]

Hatecraft: Far enough, Regina! Do what you want to me, but by the conflagration of Rogaron, you will not hurt my friends!

[Hatecraft prepares a martial arts attack but the Obliteratrix knocks him down. Shaggy and Scooby swing down from a chandelier but the Obliteratrix uses a whip to knock them down too.]

Obliteratrix: Now, where were we?

Angel: [appears] I was about to kick your sorry butt outta here. [jumps down]

[The Obliteratrix attacks with a whip, but Angel cuts it with a disc. They fight with bos, but the Obliteratrix takes out grenades and the explosion knocks Angel down the hole. The Obliteratrix peers down the hole but Angel, grabbing on the edge, throws another disc, cutting the chandelier above the Obliteratrix. The chandelier falls on the Obliteratrix and traps her inside. Mystery Inc. gets out of their nets.]

Hatecraft: Now, Regina, time to come clean and reveal that you're... [pulls off mask]

Mystery Inc.: Alice May?!

Hatecraft: Who's Alice May?

Daphne: She once pretended to be a ghost girl to kidnap Fred for her man-posse because she wanted revenge for her father, the Creeper!

Shaggy: But, like, how did you get out of jail?

Alice: I got out with the help of the same person who sent me to destroy you: Mr. E!

All: Huh?

Alice: E enlisted my services to put you kids in danger in hopes of drawing out his enemy, Professor Pericles. [flashback starts] He figured if Pericles thought you were in trouble, he'd come to your rescue. E knew if he could get Pericles to reveal himself, it'd leave his piece of the Planispheric Disk vulnerable. Everything was fake with special effects.

Shaggy: But like, how did you get all the high-tech stuff? How'd you disappear?

Alice: E took care of that. It was all courtesy of one of Destroido's shell corporations, Quest Research Laboratories. They supplied me with everything I needed: weapons, a high-tech cloaking device, even the effects. [ends flashback]

Angel: [cuffs Alice] So this was all staged by Mr. E to use the kids as... parrot bait.

Alice: That's right, and it would have worked, too, if I hadn't been stopped by you, Ms. Meddling Sassypants!

EXT. Chapel - Night
[The sheriff drives Alice away]

Sheriff: Wait, so are you tellin' me that you escaped from prison months ago, and I never noticed? [laughs] I don't think so. [drives away]

Fred: Well, gang, another mystery solved.

Daphne: I just wished we could have done something about your job, Professor Hatecraft.

Fenk: [enters] H.P.? Oh, yoo-hoo! Oh, there you are, you dear man.

Hatecraft: Don't worry, Dean Fenk, I'm on my way to clean out my office now.

Fenk: Clean out your office? Oh, never. Haven't you heard the wonderful news? The song Char Gar Gothakon based on your novel is a huge hit in Japan! And, since Darrow College published the book, we're gonna make a fortune!

[Hatecraft gasps in wonder, then follows her into her truck.]

Hatecraft: Now, I'm giving you Regina's old office— vampire books are so done, and I'm having the Duskmobile repainted. [they drive away]

Fred: Well, Angel, looks like we owe you one.

Scooby: Yeah, you saved our tails.

Daphne: How'd you know where we were?

Velma: [sighs] It's time, Angel. I can't keep this secret anymore.

Angel: I wanted to tell you kids earlier, but... I was afraid.

Scooby: Afraid of what?

Angel: Of telling you the truth. My real name isn't Angel Dynamite. It's Cassidy Williams. I'm one of the original members of Mystery Incorporated that disappeared.

All: What?!

Angel: It was all an accident. [flashback starts] We should have never been in that condemned church. But Brad said he'd seen someone comin' and goin' at night, and... he wanted to investigate. We thought we found a treasure map, but it wasn't treasure. It was a threat, to not just our lives, but the lives our families. That thing in those caves forced us to leave Crystal Cove, or those who loved us would pay the price. [flashback ends]

Shaggy: Li... li... like, who'd threatened you?

Angel: He called himself the Freak.. the Freak of Crystal Cove. There. Now you know the truth. That's what happened to the original Mystery Incorporated, and it will happen to all of you if you don't stop! Forget about the Planispheric Disk. Give Pericles your piece or Mr. E. I don't care. The mystery is over. Let it end tonight!

Fred: You lied to us, Angel. You've been lying to us from the beginning. Why should we listen to anything you have to say to us now? This mystery isn't over until we say it's over. Come on, gang! [exits]

Angel: No. No, you don't understand. He's still out there! [they drive away, she shouts] The Freak is still out there!

[The Freak watches from above.]

Freak: The curse begun, but soon they'll see. The buried truth will end with me! [cackles]

[Credits roll]